# CODEOWNERS — file-level ownership for PR review routing.
#
# Mapping mirrors plan.md lane ownership. Update when lanes are reassigned.
#
# IMPORTANT — placeholder teams: `@lash/architects`, `@lash/editor-core-owners`,
# etc. are placeholders for the GitHub team handles that will be created when
# this repo is pushed to a remote. CODEOWNERS provides ZERO enforcement until
# (a) those teams exist on GitHub, (b) branch protection on `main` requires
# code-owner review, and (c) `Restrict who can push to matching branches` is
# enabled. Until then, treat this file as documentation, not an enforcement
# barrier — see plan.md M0/A5 follow-up.

# Core editor (chips, suggest marks, table extensions, schema)
/packages/editor-core/                  @lash/editor-core-owners

# Data contracts — load-bearing; require careful review
/packages/types/                        @lash/architects

# Cross-cutting permission engine — touched by share, mentions, chat, AI, api
/packages/rbac/                         @lash/architects

# M2 lanes
